        "@id": "https://voir.lactualite.com/evenements/a-new-role-for-westmount-s-1810-cannon-465ef1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "A New Role for Westmount’s 1810 Cannon"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "For almost a century, a pair of British military cannon from the Napoleonic era was a familiar feature of Westmount Park’s landscape. Some 20 years ago, they were removed to storage for safety reasons and faced an uncertain future. This lecture recounts the cannon’s origins and use, describes its meticulous restoration over the past decade, and highlights its new role as a proud ambassador of Westmount – both locally and at events in Montreal and surrounding areas. Doors open at 6:30 pm for light refreshments. Free for 2026 WHA members and $5 for others."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/inLanguage": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
